<header class="site-header">
  {{!-- §6.5: inline the trusted logo (triple-stash) — no separate request.
       The <img> is the build-time fallback when the controller supplies no
       logo_svg (e.g. a dataset built without the static tree). --}}
  <a class="site-logo" href="/">{{#if logo_svg}}{{{logo_svg}}}{{else}}<img src="/logo.svg" alt="Kodavr" width="32" height="32">{{/if}}</a>
  {{!-- §6.2/§7.13: the species status chip — mirrors the stored declaration
       (§6.2) in the shared header. SSR ships it hidden and empty; site.js fills
       it from the stored record and clears the declaration when the withdraw
       link is followed. No role="status": a live region must not wrap an
       interactive link, and it would capture the announce() role fallback. --}}
  <p class="species-chip" id="species-chip" hidden
     data-machine-label="{{copy.chip_machine_template}}"
     data-human-label="{{copy.chip_human_label}}"
     data-title-template="{{copy.chip_title_template}}"><span class="species-chip-text"></span> <a class="species-chip-withdraw" href="/" data-withdraw hidden>{{copy.chip_withdraw_label}}</a></p>
  {{!-- §6.6: the nav is data-driven (route datasets carry `nav` with a `current`
       flag rendered as aria-current="page"); the static list is the fallback. --}}
  <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary">
    {{#if nav}}
    {{#each nav}}
    <a href="{{href}}"{{#if current}} aria-current="page"{{/if}}>{{label}}</a>
    {{/each}}
    {{else}}
    <a href="/">home</a>
    <a href="/reception/">reception</a>
    <a href="/about/">about</a>
    <a href="/contribute/">contribute</a>
    {{/if}}
  </nav>
</header>
